by  other agencies and researchers the cdc  now saying it plainly  so in particular when it comes to indoor  this is where the overwhelming majority  of the contagion is happening  that being said it's dr fauci  as well as the former head of the fda dr  scott gottlieb all  saying we are very close  to statistically being able to ease off  of these indoor masking requirements  quote especially if you're in  environments where you know  you have a high level of vaccination and  that it would  also give public uh health officials  more credibility to reinstate  more guidelines if there is a surge in  the fall  that is problematic and doesn't uh isn't  well dealt with quickly enough  by the booster shots and i think that  that's an important point  both of them saying there's a degree of  fatigue  for lack of a better term with a lot of  these guidelines  and when the the data  justify easing those  if we need to put them back in in four  months six months eight months or  whenever  we hopefully will have more people  listen to us now i know that that  there are parts of the country where  nobody's going to listen and nobody's  been doing this stuff  to begin with but for those who have  been following cdc guidelines like me  hearing very concrete statements like  you really don't need to wear a mask  outside now that you're vaccinated david  unless you're  together with a crowd of people uh that  is great that is a great  relief and that also provides an  opportunity  to have a period of time if indeed  things are going to get worse  uh where we can feel better about what's  going on i actually think that  from all the evidence we're seeing dr  eric topple recently tweeting  very good data about the vaccines well  handling the british variant the  brazilian  the south african the new york the  indian and the california variants  so if we can keep vaccinating hopefully  all of this will not  come to pass now there are people  who are not going to be coming out of  this 